# Map Styles Without Tokens

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:plotly_ex, "~> 0.3"},
  {:kino, "~> 0.18"}
])
```

## Choose a base map

Plotly.js v4 uses MapLibre-backed `Scattermap`, `Densitymap`, and
`Choroplethmap` traces with `layout.map`. These tile styles need no access token:
`open-street-map`, `carto-positron`, and `carto-darkmatter`. Tile providers still
require network access. `white-bg` uses no external tiles.

```elixir
alias Plotly.{Figure, Scattermap}

for style <- ["open-street-map", "carto-positron", "carto-darkmatter", "white-bg"] do
  Figure.new()
  |> Figure.add_trace(Scattermap.new(
    lat: [40.7128, 40.7306], lon: [-74.0060, -73.9352],
    text: ["Lower Manhattan", "Queens"], mode: "markers", marker: %{size: 14}
  ))
  |> Figure.update_layout(
    title: "Map style: #{style}", height: 360,
    map: %{style: style, center: %{lat: 40.72, lon: -73.97}, zoom: 10}
  )
  |> Plotly.show()
end
|> Kino.Layout.grid(columns: 2)
```
